The MIT license above covers this project's OWN work: the engine, the
per-language rule modules and .jsonc manifests, the hand-authored tables, the
in-repo gold referees, and the tools.

It does NOT cover every file in the repository. This repo also ships and
distributes data derived from third-party sources, each of which keeps its own
parent license — CC-BY-SA, CC-BY, CC0, Apache-2.0, BSD, two GPL-lineage data
files, and one bespoke (permissive, attribution-mandatory) grant. Those are
fenced per file.

  - LICENSES/PROVENANCE.md  — which artifact, which upstream, which license
  - LICENSES/                — the full text of every license involved
  - NOTICE.md                — the attribution roll-up

If you are redistributing, read LICENSES/PROVENANCE.md first: an MIT-only
distribution has to exclude the fenced data, which that document maps.
